<title>BRAZIL: Soy shipping conditions at key Brazilian ports.</title>
<headline>Soy shipping conditions at key Brazilian ports.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian ports of Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for shipping soybeans and soy products:</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>Vessels: (On June 5) Breeze loading 48,360 tonnes soymeal. Grl. Madalinsky loading 32,525 tonnes soymeal. Ossolineum loading 55,000 soybeans. San Giovanni loading 6,000 tonnes soyoil.</p>
<p>Waiting to dock, five vessels to load soymeal, two for soybeans and one for mixed cargo.</p>
<p>Road: no figures available.</p>
<p>Loading: no figures available.</p>
<p>Stocks: no figures available.</p>
<p>SANTOS:</p>
<p>Vessels: At public terminal, Narwick II loading 27,000 tonnes soymeal. Waiting to dock, Pythagoras of Samo to load 36,000 tonnes soybeans and Jin Pu Hai to load 54,000 tonnes soybeans.</p>
<p>At Cargill private terminal, Lika loading 60,000 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>Waiting to dock, Reduta Ordona to load 27,000 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>Road: 132 trucks carrying 3,520 tonnes soybeans arrived on June 5 as well as three trucks with 74 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>Rail: 21 wagons arrived carrying 1,106 tonnes soybeans.</p>
<p>Loading: 2,783 tonnes soybeans, 2,849 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>Stocks: 85,510 tonnes soybeans, 25,043 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
